  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nBulkhead DRB102 - firewall (section A) 35: MRS EPS pump logic enable - fuse box LOGIC MRS 7.5A (fed from k_eps_en 87, ignition-switched); moved from bulkhead B c14 2026-09-28 (the pump's ECU signal is A27)\nsp_5v (Splice): +5V at ECU A (A32 lead 18 AWG) - feeds sp_5v_bha before bulkhead A (c2, c39, c40 at 20 AWG), an 18 AWG trunk to sp_5v_b on ST185-B-cabin (broken off), crossover (a), and an 18 AWG link to sp_5v_2\nsp_5v_2 (Splice): +5V cabin loads off sp_5v - APS, cruise ladder, w210 (20 AWG each)\nsp_gndout (Splice): Gnd Out at ECU A (A24 lead 18 AWG) - feeds sp_gnd_bha before bulkhead A (c3, c41-c44 at 20 AWG) for the A loads only; loom B's sensors return to their own Gnd Out, ECU B22 (no A24-B22 tie in the harness)\nsp_sw12 (Splice): switched 12V bus - its B-side load (VSS feed on bulkhead B c20) is drawn on ST185-B-cabin (broken off); relay coil+ feeds come from sp_cp_sw12 inside the fuse box (ST185-CabinPower)\nsp_chassis (Splice): cabin chassis ground - ECU-B B25/B34 join it on ST185-B-cabin (broken off)\nsp_shield_a (Splice): drain T-splice about 6 mm (0.25 in) behind the ECU-A plug (Daniel 2026-10-12). The crank drain is the one crimped into A7 (w_drain_ecu_a is its last few mm); every other loom-A drain (cam, turbo, flex, ETB sensor, APS, front WS spur) is soldered onto it where 6 mm of its insulation is cut away. Drains stay 20/22 AWG - no combined-gauge pigtail, one wire per pin.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 5220,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_aps",
      "text": "APS PEDAL - folded in 2026-10-11 (harness-reconcile pass step 2, \"pedal is one cable in A-cabin\"): ST185-APS-Pedal.harness and its DT06-6S/DT04-6P inline mate (IX_APS) are retired; the BRZ e-throttle pedal's Sumitomo TS 025 plug is wired directly from this file. 5 of 6 pins (VC2, GND2, VC1, GND1, VPA1 -> A14) are ECU-A signals, wired straight from here; the 6th (VPA2 -> ECU-B B33) still breaks off to ST185-B-cabin (br_w39) since it's a B-letter signal - same crossover as before, just without the intermediate connector. Colours follow the former inline mate's. Run length to the pedal is still a placeholder (was 150 mm pedal-to-inline on APS-Pedal; now pedal-to-dash) - TBD, measure at the car.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 5220,
        "y": 1050
      },
      "width": 390
    },
    {
      "id": "n_drb102",
      "width": 390,
      "color": "Orange",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1110,
        "y": -180
      },
      "text": "BULKHEAD = ONE DRB102 CONNECTOR (Daniel 2026-10-12, shared-connector rule). bh_a_fw is the whole 102-cavity receptacle with TE's cavity numbers. A and B are only our names for its sections. Cavities marked N/C here are wired on ST185-B-cabin - see ST185-B-cabin (DRB 3-8, 43, 48-49, 54-55, 60, 62-102); their contacts and sealing plugs are counted there."
    }
  ],
